WEBVTT

00:00:21.477 --> 00:00:23.740
Oh, God, Oh, God.
Oh, no. No, no, no, no, no.

00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:26.221
This is bad. This is very bad.
I'm not supposed to be here.

00:00:26.264 --> 00:00:28.092
I have a pottery class at 0900!

00:00:28.136 --> 00:00:30.094
Hey, just calm down.
We don't know what this is.

00:00:30.138 --> 00:00:33.054
Are you kidding me?! Creepy
stone walls, jagged metal bars.

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:35.447
This has alien prison
written all over it.

00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:36.666
A prison?
Nah. No way, man.

00:00:36.709 --> 00:00:39.103
-This is a dungeon.
-That's even worse!

00:00:39.147 --> 00:00:41.845
Hello? Can someone give us
some context in here, please?

00:00:41.888 --> 00:00:44.630
A dungeon?! But we
didn't do anything. Did we?

00:00:44.674 --> 00:00:45.892
Oh.

00:00:45.936 --> 00:00:47.981
I've been replicating
a lot of ice.

00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:49.113
Are we not supposed to do that?

00:00:49.157 --> 00:00:50.375
I really like ice.

00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:51.550
I saw the captain
and the bridge crew

00:00:51.594 --> 00:00:52.769
get taken into another room.

00:00:52.812 --> 00:00:54.771
What if they
were replicating ice, too?!

00:00:54.814 --> 00:00:56.512
Guys, this is basically a resort

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:58.035
compared to what
the Klingons do to you.

00:00:58.079 --> 00:00:59.428
I'm sure it's not a big...

00:02:23.903 --> 00:02:25.905
-Uh, hi?
-Oh, man,

00:02:25.949 --> 00:02:27.646
they have all of our commanders
suspended in a beam!

00:02:29.213 --> 00:02:31.346
-They must be on trial.
-For what?

00:02:34.218 --> 00:02:36.742
Fellow Primes!

00:02:36.786 --> 00:02:40.093
These Federation witnesses
have been brought before you

00:02:40.137 --> 00:02:41.704
to speak truth

00:02:41.747 --> 00:02:43.575
about the senior officers

00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:47.275
of the Federation starship
Cerritos.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.887
I-I didn't witness anything.
Did you?

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.062
I don't know. What's the
difference between witnessing

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.368
and just lookin' at something?

00:02:53.411 --> 00:02:56.893
You will speak only
into the Horn of Candor!

00:02:59.156 --> 00:03:02.203
With this horn,
one of our most sacred horns,

00:03:02.246 --> 00:03:05.162
you must only speak the truth.

00:03:05.206 --> 00:03:06.642
Happy to be here.

00:03:06.685 --> 00:03:07.991
I-I don't even know
what we're supposed

00:03:08.034 --> 00:03:09.253
to be telling the truth about.

00:03:09.297 --> 00:03:12.125
The first to give testimony
will be

00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:14.824
Ensign Beckett Mariner.

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:17.000
Ship logs state
you were present on the bridge

00:03:17.043 --> 00:03:20.003
when the Cerritosmade contact
with the Clicket ship Tweerk

00:03:20.046 --> 00:03:24.312
on stardate 57818.4.

00:03:24.355 --> 00:03:27.445
Uh, I was, but I don't know
what you want me to...

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:29.926
Tell us
of those wondrous events!

00:03:29.969 --> 00:03:32.494
Okay. It started off
as a usual day.

00:03:32.537 --> 00:03:35.105
We were just hanging out.
I mean, we were just doing work

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.541
in the repair bay.

00:03:36.585 --> 00:03:39.196
Roga Danar?
Are you nuts?

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.503
I said "Who's
the all-time biggest badass?"

00:03:41.546 --> 00:03:43.287
not "Who's a dude
nobody's heard about?"

00:03:43.331 --> 00:03:45.028
Uh, everyone knows Roga Danar.

00:03:45.071 --> 00:03:47.291
-No, they don't.
-He totally outsmarted Picard,

00:03:47.335 --> 00:03:48.597
and he has amazing hair!

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.425
Well, what about Khan, right?

00:03:50.468 --> 00:03:52.949
Khan was a genetically
engineered supervillain!

00:03:52.992 --> 00:03:54.690
Dude was a space seed.

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.344
Ooh, ooh, pause for a second.
I want to talk about Khan

00:03:56.387 --> 00:03:58.433
and that thicc, thicc chest,
but I got to pee.

00:03:58.476 --> 00:04:00.783
-Roga Danar.

00:04:00.826 --> 00:04:02.785
-Get the  out of my face.-

00:04:02.828 --> 00:04:04.439
Guys, the ship's at red alert.

00:04:04.482 --> 00:04:05.483
Uh, no, it isn't.

00:04:05.527 --> 00:04:06.876
Yeah, that's impossible.

00:04:06.919 --> 00:04:08.965
I messed with our speakers
so they'd be extra loud

00:04:09.008 --> 00:04:10.532
during a red alert.
We'd know for sure.

00:04:10.575 --> 00:04:13.709
You messed
with the red alert speakers?

00:04:17.582 --> 00:04:19.497
Uh, it's, like, red alert
everywhere except here!

00:04:19.541 --> 00:04:20.933
-Rutherford!
-Aw, man.

00:04:20.977 --> 00:04:22.718
Oh, we're gonna get
in such big trouble for this.

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:23.980
We have to get to our stations!

00:04:25.547 --> 00:04:27.592
Gah, why did we have
to have bridge duty today?

00:04:27.636 --> 00:04:28.941
We're gonna walk in
and everyone's gonna be

00:04:28.985 --> 00:04:31.030
-lookin' at us.
-No, they won't. Just chill.

00:04:31.074 --> 00:04:32.597
Okay, we'll just explain what
happened and why we're late.

00:04:32.641 --> 00:04:33.859
It'll-it'll be fine.

00:04:33.903 --> 00:04:35.208
You want Rutherford fired?
No.

00:04:35.252 --> 00:04:36.601
Just follow my lead, all right?
We'll fake it.

00:04:36.645 --> 00:04:38.168
-Fake what?!
-It!

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:39.300
I'm not faking on the bridge.

00:04:39.343 --> 00:04:40.692
That's insane!

00:04:40.736 --> 00:04:41.650
The captain already knows
what she wants you to do,

00:04:41.693 --> 00:04:43.042
so just nod and agree with her,

00:04:43.086 --> 00:04:44.566
or we'll all end up
getting kicked off the ship

00:04:44.609 --> 00:04:45.871
and then we'll have
to live on Earth,

00:04:45.915 --> 00:04:47.264
where there's nothing to do
except drink wine

00:04:47.308 --> 00:04:49.179
and hang out at vineyards
and soul food restaurants!

00:04:51.399 --> 00:04:53.488
Ugh, these guys are maniacs.

00:04:53.531 --> 00:04:54.837
Captain, what happened?

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.361
They just randomly attacked me
for thanking them.

00:04:57.405 --> 00:05:00.538
This injustice will not stand.

00:05:00.582 --> 00:05:02.584
We gave you the map,
and now you turn on us?!

00:05:02.627 --> 00:05:05.238
Captain, this is all
a misunderstanding.

00:05:05.282 --> 00:05:08.720
I simply showed gratitude for
your map of the Neutral Zone.

00:05:08.764 --> 00:05:10.505
Gratitude?!
How dare you!

00:05:10.548 --> 00:05:11.680
-: Who is this guy?
-Who cares, man?

00:05:11.723 --> 00:05:12.855
Bug alien.
Roll with it.

00:05:12.898 --> 00:05:14.378
I meant no offense.

00:05:14.422 --> 00:05:16.380
I think your people have
a different definition

00:05:16.424 --> 00:05:17.381
of "gratitude."

00:05:17.425 --> 00:05:19.470
Give us back the map!

00:05:19.514 --> 00:05:21.907
Ugh, this guy is really buggin'!

00:05:21.951 --> 00:05:23.387
Mariner, what do you think?

00:05:23.431 --> 00:05:25.302
I think you know exactly how
to handle this, Captain.

00:05:25.346 --> 00:05:26.782
You're right about that.

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:28.958
Ensign Boimler,
I want options.

00:05:29.001 --> 00:05:30.960
Uh, about the-- this alien guy?

00:05:31.003 --> 00:05:32.353
Yes. Obviously.

00:05:32.396 --> 00:05:34.920
Uh, what specifically do
you wish to know?

00:05:34.964 --> 00:05:36.357
Aw, come on, man!

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.402
This is your chance to prove
you got what it takes!

00:05:38.446 --> 00:05:40.491
Oh! Well,
I-I don't know, uh, who, uh--

00:05:40.535 --> 00:05:41.492
Well, the truth is...

00:05:41.536 --> 00:05:43.015
Uh, I think we should do,

00:05:43.059 --> 00:05:45.496
uh, what you want to do, Cap'n.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.541
Cap'n's choice.

00:05:46.584 --> 00:05:48.891
I'm not asking you
to kiss my ass.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.588
Come on.
No wrong answers.

00:05:50.632 --> 00:05:52.808
Uh, okay.
We could do evasive maneuver

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:53.809
eighty...

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:55.767
eight...?

00:05:55.811 --> 00:05:57.508
Is he ing serious?

00:05:57.552 --> 00:05:58.770
That was the wrong answer!

00:05:58.814 --> 00:06:00.468
-I meant 84.
-In thissituation?

00:06:00.511 --> 00:06:02.165
-Are you crazy?
-Mariner!

00:06:02.208 --> 00:06:03.558
Have you
not been paying attention?

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:04.820
That could get us killed.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.387
: No, no, no, no.
I was kidding.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.694
Let's just-- Let's use the
impulse drive to... Crazy Ivan.

00:06:09.738 --> 00:06:12.131
-Ugh! Who the hell
is he talking about?
-What in the world is that?!

00:06:12.175 --> 00:06:14.133
-What?
-That's insane.
-But-but-but-but...

00:06:14.177 --> 00:06:16.005
Son,
you're embarrassing yourself.

00:06:16.048 --> 00:06:18.311
You got a lot to learn.
Mariner,

00:06:18.355 --> 00:06:20.923
why don't you send
our friends a message.

00:06:20.966 --> 00:06:22.751
Good call, Captain.

00:06:25.362 --> 00:06:26.972
-What?!
-Are you insane?!
-What the hell are you doing?!

00:06:27.016 --> 00:06:28.844
You said "Send them a message."
That means phasers!

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:30.889
It means to send them a message
to invite them to dinner!

00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:32.151
No, it doesn't!

00:06:32.195 --> 00:06:34.806
Target their bridge!

00:06:35.807 --> 00:06:37.243
-CLAR: Stop! Stop!

00:06:37.287 --> 00:06:38.549
What are you talking about?!

00:06:38.593 --> 00:06:39.985
What? I'm just telling you
what happened.

00:06:40.029 --> 00:06:42.466
You expect me to believe
a Starfleet officer

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.686
wouldn't know what's going on
with their ship

00:06:44.729 --> 00:06:46.296
at all times?!

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.254
Look, I'm not proud of it,
but yeah.

00:06:48.298 --> 00:06:49.647
What about the map?

00:06:49.691 --> 00:06:50.909
Tell me about the map!

00:06:50.953 --> 00:06:51.997
Uh, there was a map?

00:06:52.041 --> 00:06:53.912
That's the most important part!

00:06:53.956 --> 00:06:56.001
Dude, look, I work
on a spaceship, all right?

00:06:56.045 --> 00:06:58.917
We don't have maps.
We have stellar cartography.

00:06:58.961 --> 00:07:00.571
What is wrong with you?!

00:07:00.615 --> 00:07:02.573
Place her
in the Tank of Contempt!

00:07:06.447 --> 00:07:08.318
Oh! We got eels.
There's eels over here.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:09.580
Mariner's not lying!
I was there!

00:07:09.624 --> 00:07:10.712
We didn't see a map!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.500
Perhaps this is
a misunderstanding.

00:07:16.544 --> 00:07:18.502
You may go un-eeled.

00:07:18.546 --> 00:07:19.764
For now.

00:07:19.808 --> 00:07:22.158
Better luck next time, eels.

00:07:22.201 --> 00:07:24.552
Why does this guy care so muchabout a map of the Neutral Zone?

00:07:24.595 --> 00:07:26.075
Yeah, it's so neutral.

00:07:26.118 --> 00:07:27.990
Yeah, like, what would you
even do with a map like that?

00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:29.600
I have no idea.

00:07:29.644 --> 00:07:31.776
Ensign Samanthan Rutherford,

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.517
perhaps you
can illuminate me more

00:07:33.561 --> 00:07:35.650
than your unobservant
compatriots.

00:07:35.693 --> 00:07:37.565
Um, well, I mean,
my cyborg implant

00:07:37.608 --> 00:07:39.392
does give me perfect memory.

00:07:39.436 --> 00:07:40.785
That will be of great use!

00:07:40.829 --> 00:07:46.530
Tell me of stardate 57791.1.

00:07:46.574 --> 00:07:49.402
All right.
Stardate 5779, eh-- Hey.

00:07:49.446 --> 00:07:50.882
Wait, are you sure
you want that one?

00:07:50.926 --> 00:07:53.798
Just 'cause I haveso many great stardates in here.

00:07:53.842 --> 00:07:55.496
Other than that one.

00:07:55.539 --> 00:07:56.975
I want the one I said!

00:07:57.019 --> 00:07:59.674
Uh, you're not gonna like it.

00:07:59.717 --> 00:08:00.675
So, there I was,

00:08:00.718 --> 00:08:02.459
rotating the EPS capacitors.

00:08:02.503 --> 00:08:03.982
See, they overheat
when you leave them

00:08:04.026 --> 00:08:05.506
facing one direction too long.

00:08:05.549 --> 00:08:08.247
♪ Rotate, rotate,
rotating all day long♪

00:08:08.291 --> 00:08:09.727
-♪ While singing
my rotation...♪
-Ah. There he is!

00:08:09.771 --> 00:08:11.512
Hey, sirs!
You want to rotate with me?

00:08:11.555 --> 00:08:12.730
Maybe sing a little song?

00:08:12.774 --> 00:08:14.166
If you heard the one earlier...

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.908
No! Does your implant
have Romulan flight manuals

00:08:16.952 --> 00:08:18.519
-and repair information?
-Uh, not right now.

00:08:18.562 --> 00:08:20.564
-I'd need to update it.
-Then do it. Now!

00:08:20.608 --> 00:08:23.393
Uh, well, usually I like
to update it while I'm asleep

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:25.047
'cause it kind of messes
with my...

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:28.006
-No! Do it now!
-You do it right this second!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.313
-Okeydokey.

00:08:30.356 --> 00:08:31.967
IMPLANT:
30 seconds until restart.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.969
-Is it done yet?!
-What? No. It just started.

00:08:34.012 --> 00:08:35.536
While we wait, I'll fill you in
on the plan.

00:08:35.579 --> 00:08:37.363
Oh, uh, first off:
do you have all your shots?

00:08:37.407 --> 00:08:39.757
-Wait. Which shots?
Like, with needles?
-Ten seconds.

00:08:39.801 --> 00:08:41.498
Wait, wait, wait.
Hold on. Let me just...

00:08:41.542 --> 00:08:43.587
We don't want you getting
Dinobulan flesh-eating bacteria

00:08:43.631 --> 00:08:45.546
-on your pe...
-Hold up just a second.
My implant is also...

00:08:45.589 --> 00:08:47.635
-It'll eat right
through your underpants.
-My what?!

00:08:47.678 --> 00:08:49.375
I've seen it happen.
Terrible way to die.

00:08:49.419 --> 00:08:50.942
-Restarting Rutherford.
-Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:08:50.986 --> 00:08:53.902
-Wait, wait, wait.

00:08:55.207 --> 00:08:58.297
Whoa. I think I blacked out

00:08:58.341 --> 00:09:00.517
and lost a little bit of time
during that update.

00:09:00.561 --> 00:09:03.215
Great work nerve-pinching
those Vulcans, baby bear.

00:09:03.259 --> 00:09:05.174
Who knew you'd be better
at it than they are?

00:09:05.217 --> 00:09:07.306
-I did? But I don't know how
to nerve-pinch.
-Ha!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.395
Tell that to Spock and Spock.

00:09:09.439 --> 00:09:10.614
Oh, when my implant
was rebooting,

00:09:10.658 --> 00:09:12.137
it must have taken control.

00:09:12.181 --> 00:09:14.270
We're entering the atmosphere.
Brace for turbulence.

00:09:14.313 --> 00:09:16.054
Sirs, you don't understand.
I don't know what's going on.

00:09:16.098 --> 00:09:18.883
When we're in the museum, our
window's gonna be really tight.

00:09:18.927 --> 00:09:21.103
-Museum?
-We have to deploy now!

00:09:21.146 --> 00:09:23.453
-No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

00:09:25.934 --> 00:09:28.589
Verifying update. System will
restart in three seconds.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.119
-Ah! Romulan Bird-of-Prey?
-SHAXS: Quiet!

00:09:39.556 --> 00:09:41.689
We don't want
to draw any attention.

00:09:41.732 --> 00:09:44.387
-From who? What are we doing?
What's happening?
-Hey!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.780
What are you two doing
back here?

00:09:45.823 --> 00:09:47.216
You've drawn my attention.

00:09:47.259 --> 00:09:48.696
Distract him
with the fan dance!

00:09:48.739 --> 00:09:51.046
I'm sorry. My what now?

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:54.658
-Dance, boy! Dance!
-Ooh. Ooh. Yeah.

00:09:54.702 --> 00:09:56.225
Feels good, feels right...

00:09:56.268 --> 00:09:58.749
Hey! Stop that!
Now you're distracting me!

00:09:58.793 --> 00:10:02.057
Right. Right.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.972
I want the regular fan dance!

00:10:04.015 --> 00:10:05.147
What are you doing?!

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.714
My best.

00:10:06.757 --> 00:10:08.846
IMPLANT:
Verifying download.

00:10:11.022 --> 00:10:12.371
Aah! What the heck?!

00:10:12.415 --> 00:10:16.288
Hello? How am I standing
in space?

00:10:16.332 --> 00:10:19.857
-Huh?

00:10:19.901 --> 00:10:22.555
Ah.

00:10:22.599 --> 00:10:25.123
Cloaked Bird-of-Prey.
Wait. Did I steal this?!

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:27.909
-Aah, Mark Twain's got a gun!-Billups! Oh, man, are you okay?

00:10:27.952 --> 00:10:30.433
-Tasha, no!
The garbage bag's behind you!
-Oh, no.

00:10:30.476 --> 00:10:32.304
Sir,
you have nitrogen intoxication.

00:10:32.348 --> 00:10:33.871
You only have 60 seconds
of air left!

00:10:36.918 --> 00:10:39.311
Stop goofing around!
Get in here!

00:10:39.355 --> 00:10:40.835
Verifying update.
System restart in ten seconds.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.623
Watch it!
No, no, no, over there!

00:10:46.667 --> 00:10:49.757
Stupid... cloaked Bird.

00:10:51.759 --> 00:10:53.108
-Updating Klingon fonts.
-What?!

00:10:53.151 --> 00:10:54.587
-Why do I even need that?

00:10:54.631 --> 00:10:56.111
SHAXS:
Watch out for the controls!

00:10:56.154 --> 00:10:58.287
They're set to...

00:11:05.947 --> 00:11:07.992
Gorn wedding!

00:11:10.081 --> 00:11:12.605
Aah! Get me out of here,
implant!

00:11:12.649 --> 00:11:14.738
Nice try, Gorns!

00:11:19.874 --> 00:11:21.527
It's still the Gorn wedding?

00:11:21.571 --> 00:11:24.487
Ouch. Help! Help!
Come on, Gorns, please!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:25.793
CLAR:
A Gorn wedding?!

00:11:25.836 --> 00:11:27.838
How has this become
about a Gorn wedding?!

00:11:27.882 --> 00:11:29.492
What are you avoiding?

00:11:29.535 --> 00:11:30.885
Look, I'm just telling you
the events

00:11:30.928 --> 00:11:33.061
of stardate 57791.1, all right?

00:11:33.104 --> 00:11:34.802
Damn. Rude.

00:11:34.845 --> 00:11:38.066
I want details on how
you stole the Bird-of-Prey!

00:11:38.109 --> 00:11:39.328
I know, man. Me, too!

00:11:39.371 --> 00:11:41.069
Wait. Why would Shaxs
make him steal

00:11:41.112 --> 00:11:43.506
some old Bird-of-Prey? What
would they even do with that?

00:11:43.549 --> 00:11:46.465
Beats me. I mean,
it could be for anything.

00:11:46.509 --> 00:11:48.293
Like, who even knows?

00:11:48.337 --> 00:11:50.774
-Take him!

00:11:50.818 --> 00:11:52.515
Eels?!

00:11:52.558 --> 00:11:53.951
Dude, are you not
paying attention?

00:11:53.995 --> 00:11:56.127
-Hey! Leave them alone!
-Oh?

00:11:56.171 --> 00:11:57.955
Well, perhaps you,
Ensign D'vana Tendi,

00:11:57.999 --> 00:12:02.003
can prove more illuminating.

00:12:07.443 --> 00:12:09.358
Oh, I've always wanted
to testify about stuff!

00:12:09.401 --> 00:12:10.925
This is so cool!

00:12:10.968 --> 00:12:12.361
Hi, everyone!

00:12:12.404 --> 00:12:13.797
Don't talk to them!

00:12:13.841 --> 00:12:16.408
Have you
and Commander Jack Ransom

00:12:16.452 --> 00:12:19.063
ever set foot
in the Romulan Neutral Zone?

00:12:19.107 --> 00:12:20.804
I can't tell you that.

00:12:20.848 --> 00:12:23.328
Oh, come on!
This is an easy one!

00:12:23.372 --> 00:12:26.027
Why are you making this
so difficult?

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.507
-Tendi, just tell him
what he wants!

00:12:28.551 --> 00:12:30.901
All right, fine! But this was
a classified mission,

00:12:30.945 --> 00:12:32.860
so I'll have
to leave some things out.

00:12:32.903 --> 00:12:36.385
I had just been given
a major assignment.

00:12:36.428 --> 00:12:38.300
Mariner! Mariner, guess what?

00:12:38.343 --> 00:12:39.910
I get to tidy
the conference rooms!

00:12:39.954 --> 00:12:41.651
Ah! What should I wear?

00:12:41.694 --> 00:12:43.392
Probably just my uniform, right?

00:12:43.435 --> 00:12:45.481
Ugh! How are you so excited?

00:12:45.524 --> 00:12:47.788
You know you're just gonna be
wiping cat fur off chairs.

00:12:47.831 --> 00:12:48.876
Uh, do you know how many
big decisions happen

00:12:48.919 --> 00:12:50.181
in those conference rooms?

00:12:50.225 --> 00:12:51.487
That's where
they talk about the Borg.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:52.923
You can talk about the Borg
anywhere.

00:12:52.967 --> 00:12:55.273
Yeah, but when you do it
in a conference room,

00:12:55.317 --> 00:12:58.189
it becomes a conference.

00:12:58.233 --> 00:13:01.453
I never get
to clean the conference room.

00:13:03.499 --> 00:13:05.806
Wow.

00:13:05.849 --> 00:13:07.546
The captain's chair.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.853
Oh, I'm gonna make you
extra clean. Huh?

00:13:09.897 --> 00:13:11.724
Secure the room,
Lieutenant .

00:13:11.768 --> 00:13:13.857
-Yes, sir.
-CLAR: Okay, stop.

00:13:13.901 --> 00:13:16.207
You can't omit details
like that!

00:13:16.251 --> 00:13:18.775
Yeah, but I already did, so...

00:13:18.819 --> 00:13:20.777
Are you so stubborn

00:13:20.821 --> 00:13:23.562
that you're willing
to risk death by eels?

00:13:23.606 --> 00:13:25.303
Yes, that's correct.

00:13:25.347 --> 00:13:27.915
Then continue.

00:13:27.958 --> 00:13:30.482
You must be The Cleaner.

00:13:30.526 --> 00:13:32.702
Yes, sirree.
And happy to be here.

00:13:32.745 --> 00:13:34.965
Glad to have you. This
mission is highly classified.

00:13:35.009 --> 00:13:36.532
From here on out,
you're

00:13:36.575 --> 00:13:38.403
-and .
-Wow.

00:13:38.447 --> 00:13:39.927
All right, everybody,
listen up. I'm serious.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.711
This is important.
If we're captured...

00:13:41.754 --> 00:13:43.713
TENDI:
He's glad to have me!

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:46.890
Gosh, it's just so nice
to be recognized for my work.

00:13:46.934 --> 00:13:49.588
And cleaning the conference room is important. I knew it.

00:13:49.632 --> 00:13:51.242
Wait, I should be
paying attention.

00:13:51.286 --> 00:13:53.418
This is why we got
matching tattoos.

00:13:53.462 --> 00:13:54.942
-10-4.
-Lock and load.

00:13:54.985 --> 00:13:56.813
We're  for life.

00:13:56.857 --> 00:13:58.380
Check out this map.
It's gonna lead us

00:13:58.423 --> 00:14:00.904
straight into the Neutral Z...
 ...one.

00:14:00.948 --> 00:14:02.384
The Neutral what, now?

00:14:02.427 --> 00:14:03.733
RANSOM:
The package is located here.

00:14:03.776 --> 00:14:06.388
Guards are stationed
here and here on weekends.

00:14:06.431 --> 00:14:09.173
If we run into trouble,
Cleaner will extract us.

00:14:09.217 --> 00:14:11.175
Let's  this  up!

00:14:13.612 --> 00:14:15.005
Yeah...

00:14:15.049 --> 00:14:18.095
Phaser rifles.

00:14:18.139 --> 00:14:20.402
RUTHERFORD: Oh, snap!
That's the ship from my story!

00:14:20.445 --> 00:14:22.230
TENDI:  I knew
I should have made it clear

00:14:22.273 --> 00:14:23.579
that I wasn't supposed
to be there,

00:14:23.622 --> 00:14:25.755
but every time I was about to...

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:28.062
So, here is a very funny thing.

00:14:28.105 --> 00:14:31.761
Um, I think that there was
a misunderstanding,

00:14:31.804 --> 00:14:34.459
-and I...
-Everyone quiet!
They're scanning the area.

00:14:37.985 --> 00:14:39.725
-Ah...
-That was close.

00:14:39.769 --> 00:14:41.379
We're lucky we have this
Bird-of-Prey, or we'd be toast.

00:14:41.423 --> 00:14:42.815
Uh, but what
I was saying was...

00:14:42.859 --> 00:14:44.643
Shh! They're scanning again.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.865
They stopped scanning.
Cleaner, what was that?

00:14:48.909 --> 00:14:52.129
-What I was saying was...
-Oh, no, they're scanning!

00:14:52.173 --> 00:14:53.957
Okay, now they're not
scanning anymore.

00:14:54.001 --> 00:14:55.654
-Anything important... Whoa!
-What I was...

00:14:55.698 --> 00:14:57.352
REDACTED:
Stop! I'm picking up scanning!

00:14:57.395 --> 00:14:59.223
Okay, they're done scanning.
Oh, God!

00:14:59.267 --> 00:15:00.703
They're scanning again!

00:15:00.746 --> 00:15:01.878
No, no. That was on me.

00:15:01.922 --> 00:15:04.011
That was wrong. No, I wasn't!

00:15:10.408 --> 00:15:12.715
Uh, so, a-about me
being "the cleaner..."

00:15:12.758 --> 00:15:15.761
Yeah, yeah. At your age,
it's very impressive.

00:15:18.547 --> 00:15:20.853
Comm silence from here on out.

00:15:23.291 --> 00:15:25.989
TENDI:
Whoa.

00:15:26.033 --> 00:15:28.949
-You know who I hate? Remans.
-Oh, they're the worst.

00:15:28.992 --> 00:15:30.080
-TENDI: Sorry.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.736
Apologizing to the enemy?

00:15:33.779 --> 00:15:35.651
-That's cold, Cleaner.
-You're playing

00:15:35.694 --> 00:15:38.175
some real  up mind games.

00:15:45.008 --> 00:15:46.749
-Stay here, cover our six.
-Six what?

00:15:46.792 --> 00:15:47.968
Copy.

00:15:53.495 --> 00:15:54.670
Is that the package?

00:15:54.713 --> 00:15:57.238
Cleaner, do your thing!

00:15:57.281 --> 00:15:59.022
What's my thing? I have a thing?What's my thing?!

00:16:05.072 --> 00:16:07.204
Whoa, I thought she was
just supposed to beam us

00:16:07.248 --> 00:16:08.945
-out of here.
-She was.

00:16:08.989 --> 00:16:11.861
I do not know what's going
on here. This is crazy.

00:16:12.905 --> 00:16:14.516
Congrats, boys.

00:16:14.559 --> 00:16:16.431
The package is safely on board,

00:16:16.474 --> 00:16:18.650
and there's no indication
that the Rom...

00:16:18.694 --> 00:16:21.044
...ulan high council
detected us.

00:16:21.088 --> 00:16:22.524
-Yeah!

00:16:24.308 --> 00:16:27.137
Too bad we have to deny
this ever happened,

00:16:27.181 --> 00:16:29.139
because you were awesome.

00:16:30.836 --> 00:16:32.751
You,

00:16:32.795 --> 00:16:34.666
you're  crazy.

00:16:40.237 --> 00:16:42.674
This is where Billups sits.

00:16:42.718 --> 00:16:43.719
CLAR:
Stop!

00:16:43.762 --> 00:16:45.416
You expect me to believe that?

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.331
Yes, that is where Billups sits.

00:16:47.375 --> 00:16:49.855
You did not do martial arts

00:16:49.899 --> 00:16:51.814
on multiple armed guards!

00:16:51.857 --> 00:16:54.686
You're right. I didn't.

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:57.776
-I tried to be reasonable.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.169
I tried to get to the truth.

00:16:59.213 --> 00:17:02.172
Today didn't have to end
in eels!

00:17:02.216 --> 00:17:05.219
-Ignite the burners!

00:17:07.264 --> 00:17:09.005
-Oh!

00:17:09.049 --> 00:17:12.182
Why would you have burners
andeels? It's redundant!

00:17:16.491 --> 00:17:20.538
Just tell me about the package.
What was inside the package?

00:17:20.582 --> 00:17:23.280
I don't know, but whatever
it was, I'm sure it was great.

00:17:25.108 --> 00:17:27.110
I think you're hurting the eels!

00:17:27.154 --> 00:17:30.287
CLAR:
This can all be over
if you just tell me

00:17:30.331 --> 00:17:31.897
what your bridge crew did!

00:17:31.941 --> 00:17:33.290
We can't tell you.

00:17:33.334 --> 00:17:35.075
Why? Why?

00:17:35.118 --> 00:17:36.380
Because we don't know!

00:17:36.424 --> 00:17:37.903
We never know anything!

00:17:40.645 --> 00:17:41.777
We're lower decks.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.735
No one ever tells us
what's going on.

00:17:43.779 --> 00:17:44.997
We're not important enough

00:17:45.041 --> 00:17:46.521
to have anything
to lie to you about.

00:17:46.564 --> 00:17:49.089
You're Starfleet.
Surely you must be briefed

00:17:49.132 --> 00:17:50.220
on every contingency.

00:17:50.264 --> 00:17:52.179
Yeah, I wish.
The senior officers

00:17:52.222 --> 00:17:54.050
don't always have time
to keep us up to speed.

00:17:54.094 --> 00:17:56.792
Hell, sometimes, they don't
even know what's going on.

00:17:56.835 --> 00:17:58.533
Impossible!

00:17:58.576 --> 00:18:00.143
Human lies!

00:18:00.187 --> 00:18:04.016
-You are the best of the best!

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:05.801
-Your senior officers

00:18:05.844 --> 00:18:08.543
are always in full control!

00:18:08.586 --> 00:18:11.459
No, they're not.
They mess up all the time.

00:18:11.502 --> 00:18:14.288
-Like whenever Q shows up.

00:18:14.331 --> 00:18:15.985
Voilà!

00:18:17.987 --> 00:18:20.076
-Oh, what?
-Damn you, Q!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:24.080
Good luck solving
my little puzzle, mes amis.

00:18:24.124 --> 00:18:27.823
Tell me, now, can you prove
that humanity is worth saving?

00:18:27.866 --> 00:18:30.434
I think not.

00:18:32.219 --> 00:18:34.569
Well, he clearly wants us

00:18:34.612 --> 00:18:36.353
to play something.

00:18:36.397 --> 00:18:38.660
Ah! It's soccer. Okay.

00:18:38.703 --> 00:18:40.966
-Oh!
-BALL: What's humanity
all about?

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:42.925
It's puzzle time.
It's puzzle time.

00:18:42.968 --> 00:18:46.581
-Ugh. Any ideas? Anybody?
-Oh!

00:18:46.624 --> 00:18:48.278
BOIMLER: Or half of Ransom's alien dates

00:18:48.322 --> 00:18:49.845
that he doesn't do
any research for.

00:18:49.888 --> 00:18:52.326
You are so funny, Mary Anne.

00:18:52.369 --> 00:18:54.589
How about we keep this party
going in my quarters?

00:18:54.632 --> 00:18:57.157
Hey. Hey, Jack. FYI, you're
hitting on a salt vampire.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.723
- Yeah, right. Nice try.-

00:18:58.767 --> 00:19:00.986
Salt vampires died out
more than a century ago.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.293
-All right. Cool, be safe.
-Come on, Mary Anne.

00:19:03.337 --> 00:19:04.512
Let's get out of here.

00:19:04.555 --> 00:19:07.906
I'll give you the tour
of casa de Ransom.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.039
- Salt vampire!

00:19:10.082 --> 00:19:12.128
-CLAR: You're making this up.
-BOIMLER: Nuh-uh.

00:19:12.172 --> 00:19:14.304
I read all their logs. They're
stepping in it all the time.

00:19:14.348 --> 00:19:16.263
Captain. Captain!

00:19:16.306 --> 00:19:18.090
Someone is replacing
everyone on the ship

00:19:18.134 --> 00:19:20.223
with imposters
who claim not to know me.

00:19:20.267 --> 00:19:21.964
We might be
in a parallel dimension.

00:19:22.007 --> 00:19:23.748
-And you are?
-Uh...

00:19:23.792 --> 00:19:26.098
Wait, is this...
is this not the Cerritos?

00:19:26.142 --> 00:19:29.363
This is the Alhambra.
Did you get on the wrong ship?

00:19:29.406 --> 00:19:32.279
They all look the same!

00:19:33.323 --> 00:19:35.020
Who the hell was that?

00:19:35.064 --> 00:19:36.892
Why are you doing this to me?

00:19:36.935 --> 00:19:38.372
I need you to tell me

00:19:38.415 --> 00:19:41.331
that your senior officers
are infallible heroes.

00:19:41.375 --> 00:19:43.942
Well, they're not.
And that's okay.

00:19:43.986 --> 00:19:45.335
We all joined Starfleet

00:19:45.379 --> 00:19:47.337
to dive headfirst
into the unknown.

00:19:47.381 --> 00:19:48.686
We're explorers.

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.906
Of course we don't always know
what's going on.

00:19:50.949 --> 00:19:52.473
Did Picard know about the Borg?

00:19:52.516 --> 00:19:55.563
Did Kirk know about
that giant Spock on Phylos?

00:19:55.606 --> 00:19:58.043
Did Dr. Crusher know about
that ghost in the lamp thing

00:19:58.087 --> 00:19:59.567
from the Scottish planet
that she hooked up with

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.090
that one time? That whole thing.

00:20:01.133 --> 00:20:03.397
You clearly want us to say
that the captain

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.746
and her crew messed up,

00:20:04.789 --> 00:20:06.965
but we simply don't have
the full story,

00:20:07.009 --> 00:20:08.706
and that's the truth!

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.622
Whatever they did, I guarantee
you it was all for good.

00:20:11.666 --> 00:20:14.059
You have shown no evidence
that they're guilty of a crime.

00:20:14.103 --> 00:20:15.887
In fact, I find youguilty

00:20:15.931 --> 00:20:18.934
of trying to take them down
with this sham of a trial!

00:20:18.977 --> 00:20:20.240
Drumhead!

00:20:22.154 --> 00:20:25.201
Wait, you think this is a trial?

00:20:25.245 --> 00:20:26.985
Uh, yes?

00:20:27.029 --> 00:20:28.248
-It's not?
-Yeah, I mean,
it's pretty trial-y.

00:20:28.291 --> 00:20:29.684
Could someone
bring up the lights?

00:20:33.253 --> 00:20:34.689
This isn't a trial.

00:20:34.732 --> 00:20:37.257
It's a party,
for this brave crew

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:39.694
who rescued me
from the Romulans.

00:20:39.737 --> 00:20:40.912
What?

00:20:40.956 --> 00:20:43.350
CLAR:
I was kidnapped by Romulans

00:20:43.393 --> 00:20:46.178
and held for over a year
until they saved me.

00:20:46.222 --> 00:20:49.747
Imperium Magistrate Clar, you'resafe now, aboard the Cerritos.

00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:53.011
Thank you, Captain Freeman.
Thank you.

00:20:53.055 --> 00:20:56.363
You must come and celebrate
with me on K'Tuevon Prime.

00:20:56.406 --> 00:20:59.801
Your deeds and my victory
will forever be etched

00:20:59.844 --> 00:21:03.065
-onto our great history stone.
-Can't say no to a party.

00:21:03.108 --> 00:21:05.459
Oh, great, guess I'll have
to shave my .

00:21:05.502 --> 00:21:06.764
Yeah, maybe you should.

00:21:08.636 --> 00:21:10.333
What's that about?

00:21:10.377 --> 00:21:12.248
I don't know, man.
Something dumb.

00:21:14.294 --> 00:21:16.992
This was supposed
to be my special day.

00:21:17.035 --> 00:21:18.428
No. No, no, no, no, no.
This is a trial.

00:21:18.472 --> 00:21:19.864
You said we were witnesses,

00:21:19.908 --> 00:21:22.127
-you said we had to testify.
-Are you stupid?

00:21:22.171 --> 00:21:23.999
How could you think
this was a trial?

00:21:24.042 --> 00:21:27.437
Because you've got our bosses
suspended in a scary-ass beam.

00:21:27.481 --> 00:21:30.092
That is the beam of celebration!

00:21:30.135 --> 00:21:32.486
It is an honor
to be in this beam.

00:21:32.529 --> 00:21:33.661
Shut up, Billups!

00:21:33.704 --> 00:21:35.184
Hey, man, this is not on us.

00:21:35.227 --> 00:21:38.143
I mean, all of that chanting,
and the-the metal gavel?

00:21:38.187 --> 00:21:40.015
This is, like, alien trial 101.

00:21:40.058 --> 00:21:42.757
You raised us up on a platform
into a creepy courtroom.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.325
Creepy? This is one
of our nicest event silos.

00:21:45.368 --> 00:21:47.849
-I got married here!
-Wh-- Well, then,
who's this judge?

00:21:47.892 --> 00:21:50.852
This guy's just been, like,
scowling at us the whole time.

00:21:50.895 --> 00:21:53.071
-I don't know him.-Whoa, whoa, whoa. I'm just here

00:21:53.115 --> 00:21:55.117
to set up for a birthday later
for my little girl.

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:57.424
-She's turning 100.
-TENDI: Aw.

00:21:57.467 --> 00:22:00.209
Okay, all right, Clar,
time's up.

00:22:00.252 --> 00:22:02.298
-Etchers down.
-But-but...

00:22:02.342 --> 00:22:04.169
we didn't even get
to do any etching.

00:22:04.213 --> 00:22:07.259
No, no, no, no. You only paid
for 22 minutes.

00:22:07.303 --> 00:22:08.652
Other people got to etch.

00:22:08.696 --> 00:22:10.088
Oh, come on.

00:22:10.132 --> 00:22:12.090
But-but wh-- Okay, what about,
what about the eels?

00:22:12.134 --> 00:22:14.441
You held us in contempt,
of eels.

00:22:14.484 --> 00:22:16.138
All right, come on.
That's enough.

00:22:16.181 --> 00:22:17.357
-You dipped us in eels!
-You ruined my party!

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:19.184
Those were eels
you dipped us in!

00:22:19.228 --> 00:22:21.186
-You did that! You did it!
-You ruined my party!

00:22:23.319 --> 00:22:26.801
Today you four almost
got yourselves killed

00:22:26.844 --> 00:22:28.542
at a thank-you dinner.

00:22:28.585 --> 00:22:30.326
But, the way you stood up
for Starfleet

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:32.023
while you thought you were
staring death in the face

00:22:32.067 --> 00:22:34.025
deserves commendation.

00:22:34.069 --> 00:22:36.201
-I guess.

00:22:37.464 --> 00:22:38.900
Going forward,
we'll make an effort

00:22:38.943 --> 00:22:40.815
to keep the crew more informed.

00:22:40.858 --> 00:22:43.905
The Cerritoswill be
synonymous with clarity.

00:22:43.948 --> 00:22:46.081
Wait, so then what did
Clar do to get captured

00:22:46.124 --> 00:22:48.344
by the Romulans?
I-I missed that part.

00:22:48.388 --> 00:22:49.998
Well, it's-it's complicated.

00:22:50.041 --> 00:22:52.174
Why did you let him
hurt us with eels

00:22:52.217 --> 00:22:54.263
if you knew it wasn't a trial?

00:22:54.306 --> 00:22:56.570
We have to honor the local
customs of alien governments.

00:22:56.613 --> 00:22:58.136
And can you tell me
who was on that secret team

00:22:58.180 --> 00:22:59.355
that infiltrated
the Neutral Zone?

00:22:59.399 --> 00:23:01.488
Uh, I'm not at liberty to...

00:23:01.531 --> 00:23:03.359
And why couldn't you just ask
the Vulcans to borrow

00:23:03.403 --> 00:23:04.708
the Bird-of-Prey?
And where did they get it?

00:23:04.752 --> 00:23:06.493
And why was that a job
for the Cerritos?

00:23:06.536 --> 00:23:08.059
Why couldn't it have just beena job for, like, the
Enterprise,

00:23:08.103 --> 00:23:09.757
-or...
-Okay, you know what?
It's classified.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.672
It's all classified. Dismissed!

00:23:11.715 --> 00:23:14.370
Hey, everybody, look, we got
Captain Clarity over here.

00:23:14.414 --> 00:23:16.111
I said dismissed!

00:23:16.154 --> 00:23:19.636
Honestly, this is fine with me.
Knowing things means more work.

00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:22.247
Well, I, for one, knew
it was a party the whole time.

00:23:22.291 --> 00:23:23.640
Yeah, right, dude.

00:23:23.684 --> 00:23:25.294
-I did.
-Then why were you crying?

00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:27.296
I just-- i-it was cold in there.

00:23:27.339 --> 00:23:29.603
I've got sensitive corneas.
I told you.

00:23:31.387 --> 00:23:33.345
I challenge you all to a duel.

00:23:33.389 --> 00:23:34.521
Pick your weapons.

00:23:34.564 --> 00:23:36.174
I pick the mind.

00:23:36.218 --> 00:23:37.306
Get out of here, Q! No.

00:23:37.349 --> 00:23:38.786
We are done
with random stuff today.

00:23:38.829 --> 00:23:40.831
We're not dealing
with any of your Q bull.

00:23:40.875 --> 00:23:42.267
Oh, s'il vous plaît, Mariner.

00:23:42.311 --> 00:23:44.226
I want to put humanity
to the ultimate test.

00:23:44.269 --> 00:23:45.532
MARINER:
Okay, I'm not French. No.

00:23:45.575 --> 00:23:47.316
-Go find Picard.
-Q: Oh, Picard.

00:23:47.359 --> 00:23:49.666
He's no fun, he's always
quoting Shakespeare,

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:51.668
he's always making wine.

00:24:27.661 --> 00:24:29.706
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:25:19.669 --> 00:25:20.670
Chirp.
